# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RestOS — CLOUD host. Copy to cloud.env, fill in from ops/ids.env, keep mode 600.
#
# Four processes live here: sync-gateway (8080), api (3001), backoffice (3000), jobs (no port).
# Each systemd unit in ops/systemd/ reads THIS ONE FILE via EnvironmentFile, so a value that two
# processes must agree on cannot drift between two files. Every variable below was derived by
# grepping process.env / defineEnv across services/ and apps/backoffice/, not from a document.
#
# Convention below: REQUIRED means the process refuses to boot without it and says so.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═══ shared by sync-gateway, api and jobs ════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The kernel Postgres.
#   sync-gateway: OPTIONAL, defaults to postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/restos, and
#                 connects LAZILY — a wrong DSN is not a boot failure here, it is a 500 on the
#                 first request that needs the database. The boot line prints (redacted) which
#                 DSN it will try, and a fourth boot line reports the schema state.
#   jobs:         REQUIRED, no default, on purpose — a nightly Auditor pointed at a database
#                 nobody named would report "ok" about the wrong ledger for ever.
# WRONG VALUE: the gateway serves sync until the first push, then 500s; the back office cannot
# publish; the Auditor audits nothing and says it is fine.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://restos:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/restos


# ═══ services/sync-gateway ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# REQUIRED. HS256 key the gateway verifies device tokens with and provision-device signs them
# with — one key, two commands, and they MUST be the same string. >= 32 BYTES, enforced at boot.
# WRONG VALUE: every device is rejected at hello. The till shows Cloud OFF and keeps selling
# offline (01-F17), so the failure is quiet on the counter and loud only in the gateway log.
# From ops/ids.env: DEVICE_TOKEN_SECRET
DEVICE_TOKEN_SECRET=

# The /internal publish credential. OPTIONAL, and ABSENT IS FAIL-CLOSED: every /internal route
# answers 503, so a gateway that was never told the credential accepts no menu from anyone.
# >= 32 bytes when set. It is the same string as SYNC_GATEWAY_TOKEN below.
# WRONG VALUE: 401 on every publish. The owner authors a menu, saves it, sees it publish in the
# back office, and no till ever receives it.
# From ops/ids.env: PUBLISH_TOKEN
PUBLISH_TOKEN=

# OPTIONAL deployment binding (01-F47). Unset = unbound; set = a token minted for staging does
# not validate against production. If you set either one here, provision-device MUST run with
# the same values in ITS environment, or it mints a perfectly-signed token that opens nothing.
# Leave both unset for a single-restaurant pilot: one more thing to get silently wrong.
# DEVICE_TOKEN_ISSUER=
# DEVICE_TOKEN_AUDIENCE=

# OPTIONAL, default 8080. Binds 0.0.0.0 in PLAIN HTTP/WS — there is no TLS in this product, so
# this port must not face the internet without a reverse proxy in front of it.
# WRONG VALUE: outside 0..65535 is a boot crash. A port already in use is an EADDRINUSE crash.
# PORT is per-process and these four processes share this file, so the gateway's port is set in
# its unit file (ops/systemd/restos-sync-gateway.service), not here.


# ═══ services/api ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# REQUIRED. Back-office session signing key. NON-EMPTY IS THE ONLY CHECK — there is no length
# floor on this one, unlike the two secrets above. Do not hand-type a short one.
# WRONG VALUE: changing it invalidates every logged-in back-office session immediately.
# From ops/ids.env: SESSION_SECRET
SESSION_SECRET=

# REQUIRED, both. Where the API publishes a menu to. The API refuses to boot without them, and
# that refusal is deliberate: an API that starts without a gateway looks completely healthy and
# ships nothing, which is this codebase's most expensive recurring failure.
# SYNC_GATEWAY_TOKEN must be byte-identical to the gateway's PUBLISH_TOKEN above.
# WRONG URL: the back office renders a named integration error (not "fetch failed") and no
# publish lands. WRONG TOKEN: 401 on every publish, same visible symptom.
SYNC_GATEWAY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
SYNC_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# 01-F60's enabled (branch, channel) set — the ONLY declaration of it anywhere. The back office
# draws its price grid from this, with no fallback, and the writer refuses a save against the
# same value. Comma-separated.
#
# ⚠ ENABLED_BRANCHES must CONTAIN the till's RESTOS_BRANCH_ID. Not equal — contain.
# ⚠ EMPTY REFUSES EVERY CATALOG SAVE. It does not mean "check nothing".
# ⚠ ENABLED_CHANNELS is a CLOSED set: counter, phone, storefront, whatsapp, foodpanda. Anything
#   else CRASHES THE API AT BOOT, naming the value — deliberately, because boot is the last
#   moment an operator can fix it before an owner types prices into a column that matches no
#   lookup that can ever happen.
# ⚠ DECIDE THIS SET BEFORE THE MENU IS AUTHORED. Adding a channel later leaves every already
#   published entry with no price on it, and each one reads "no price set" on the till until it
#   is opened and saved again. See ops/README.md, "Two menu traps".
# From ops/ids.env: BRANCH_ID
ENABLED_BRANCHES=
ENABLED_CHANNELS=counter,phone

# Where ACCOUNTS live. Set (and it IS set, at the top of this file — all four units read this one
# file) means the login path reads kernel.users: the rows `pnpm -C services/sync-gateway
# create-owner` writes, which survive a restart and which list-tenancy can report (15-F26/15-F27).
# There is nothing to add here; DATABASE_URL above is the whole configuration.
#
# The API prints TWO boot lines and the second is the one to read:
#   @restos/api accounts: kernel.users at postgres://…@… (persistent; …)
# It will also say `BOOTSTRAP_OWNER_* development seed … DIES WITH THIS PROCESS` or `NONE — …
# nobody can log in`, which are the two states that used to be invisible from outside the process.

# ⚠ THE BOOTSTRAP_OWNER_* TRIO IS THE DEVELOPMENT SEED AND MUST STAY UNSET ON THIS HOST.
# It is 15-F26's named stopgap: one owner, IN MEMORY, gone on restart, in no kernel.users row —
# so 14-F14's CRUD could never deactivate it and list-tenancy cannot report it. Setting it BESIDE
# DATABASE_URL is two answers to one question (who may sign in) and the API REFUSES TO BOOT,
# naming both. That refusal is deliberate: a precedence rule would give an operator a working
# login and no way to tell which account they were using.
#   BOOTSTRAP_ORG_ID=
#   BOOTSTRAP_OWNER_EMAIL=
#   BOOTSTRAP_OWNER_PASSWORD_HASH=
#   BOOTSTRAP_OWNER_NAME=
#
# ⚠ The org id you provision with `create-org --org <id>` must equal every device's RESTOS_ORG_ID,
#   and its branch must appear in ENABLED_BRANCHES above. NOTHING CHECKS THIS. Getting it wrong
#   gives four healthy processes and no menu, with no error anywhere.
# From ops/ids.env: ORG_ID


# ═══ services/jobs (the 20 §4.2 Auditor) ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# REQUIRED. BullMQ's backend. ioredis retries a refused connection FOR EVER, so a worker with no
# Redis boots, prints its startup lines, and never runs a single audit pass — silently.
# WRONG VALUE: no pass ever runs, and nothing says so louder than a stalled connection.
REDIS_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379

# OPTIONAL, default 86400000 (24 h). Positive integer milliseconds; anything else is a boot
# crash. Lower it only to investigate a reported discrepancy — a full-ledger refold is not free.
# AUDITOR_INTERVAL_MS=86400000


# ═══ apps/backoffice ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Where the Next server proxies /api/trpc/* to. Read PER REQUEST by the Next server and never
# inlined into the browser bundle, so the backend can be repointed by a restart, not a rebuild.
# OPTIONAL, default http://127.0.0.1:3001.
# WRONG VALUE: every back-office screen shows a named integration error. Nothing is silent here.
RESTOS_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3001
